[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Every tab, screen, section, card and figure on a page is a narrative's own declaration

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-VIEW-STRUCTURE-COMES-FROM-THE-CANON
TITLE: Every tab, screen, section, card and figure on a page is a narrative's own declaration
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Every tab, screen, section, card and figure a page shows is declared by a narrative -- its PLACE, its WIDGET, its Over target, its Contains order. The renderer adds only what has no content: the Start of a root with the check findings under it, the Nodes index, an index of screen children where a container declares none, the rows anywhere on the page that link a screen (drawn beneath it as line cards with crumbs home), previous and next over screen siblings, crumbs and routes. A renderer that derives a screen's structure from the shape of the tree violates this.
<<<
